      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Chinese transcription (FFmpeg + FunASR)\n\n## Before Queue\n1. Put the media file in `ComfyUI/input` and set **Media Input -> path** to its name (for example `video.mp4`), or enter an absolute path.\n2. For a direct URL: set **Media Input -> source_type** to `url`, paste the direct media URL, and clear or ignore `path`.\n3. Install FFmpeg. The first queue downloads the FunASR model weights (this can take several minutes).\n\n## Pipeline\nMedia Input -> Resolve Media -> Load Media -> FFmpeg Extract Audio -> FunASR Transcribe -> Format Transcript.\n\n- A local file is validated directly; a URL is downloaded to `output/transcribe/downloads`.\n- `paraformer-zh` (default here) returns sentence timestamps and punctuation, which SRT needs.\n- `iic/SenseVoiceSmall` is faster but returns no timestamps: use `txt`/`json`, or use the VAD starter for SRT.\n- `FunAudioLLM/Fun-ASR-Nano-2512` is a newer multilingual option without documented timestamps.\n\n## Output\n`ComfyUI/output/transcribe/chinese_transcript.srt`\n\nChange **Format Transcript -> format** to `txt`, `json` or `vtt`; the extension follows automatically. `max_line_chars` is a display width where Chinese characters count as 2.\n\nDirect URLs only: YouTube/Bilibili pages are HTML and are rejected. Use yt-dlp first.\n"
      ]
    }
